= Deployment =

This page describes the public content deployment model for BITwiki V2. It intentionally excludes credentials, private infrastructure, protected configuration, and other non-public operational details.

== Source ==
The public `wiki-content` repository represents the candidate public MediaWiki corpus. Namespace directories map to MediaWiki page classes; `.mediawiki` files contain wikitext.

== Deployment principles ==
# Verify the live MediaWiki version and extension set before applying content that depends on optional features.
# Import or update pages with revision-aware tooling.
# Preserve redirects and page history wherever possible.
# Rebuild Semantic MediaWiki data after schema/property changes when required.
# Verify links, templates, modules, categories, queries, and transclusions after deployment.
# Keep protected/private namespaces outside the public Git projection.

== Compatibility ==
V2 may define future namespace or extension requirements, such as a Portal namespace. Such requirements must be declared and validated before import; content should not silently depend on unavailable functionality.

